2) Strategy step-by-step, rewritten as an EA pipeline
Step 1 — Market Bias & Targets (H4)
From PDF: observe current impulsive move and candle structure; identify boundaries as targets (H/L levels, trend lines/channels). Avoid if at high/low, consolidating/erratic, low volatility/momentum.
EA implementation:
On each new H4 candle:
1. Detect bias = `BULL`, `BEAR`, or `NONE` using impulsive move logic.
2. Build a list of targets (“boundaries”):
Recent swing highs/lows
Optional: channel / trendline (harder to do robustly; usually skip or approximate with linear regression channel)
Avoid filters (must be code-defined):
Because the PDF uses human words, you must choose measurable definitions:
At a High/Low level: price within X pips/points of last N-bar swing high/low.
Consolidating: ATR below threshold OR range compression (high-low of last N H4 bars is small).
Erratic structure: too many alternating candle directions; e.g., >K direction changes in last N bars.
Low volatility/momentum: ATR low OR average candle body small.
> My strong opinion: use ATR-based gates. “Erratic structure” is subjective; define it or delete it.
---
Step 2 — Market Structure Identification (H4)
From PDF: Identify previously untouched wick levels that correlate with direction of current impulsive move. Candle conditions: previous candles must have momentum; structure impulsive not grindy.
This is the “Indication level” generator.
Code definition (practical):
A wick level is a price (high or low) from a momentum candle that has not been revisited.
For bullish bias:
Candidate indication levels = upper wick highs? (PDF says “wick levels that correlate with direction of current impulsive move”, which is vague)
In most “wick retest” systems, for bullish continuation you watch prior lows / demand wicks, not highs.
So we implement both options as a parameter:
`input bool UseWickHighsForBull = false; // default false`
Untouched wick level condition:
A wick price `L` from candle `k` is “untouched” if for all candles between `k-1` down to current:
bullish case (retest down): `Low[j] > L` (price never traded at/below L)
bearish case (retest up): `High[j] < L`
Store these in an array of `struct Level { double price; datetime time; int tf; }`
Also enforce “momentum candle” for candle `k`:
`abs(close-open) / (high-low) >= MomentumBodyRatio` AND body size > ATRX
