8) Trade management protocols as deterministic algorithms
A) Iron Dome Protocol
From PDF:
+1R: close 25%, move SL to BE
+2R: close 25%, move SL to +1R
+3R+: hold 50%, trail SL +1R for every +1R gain
Code definition:
Let:
`R = abs(entry - SL_initial)` in price terms
Current profit in R:
bullish: `(Bid - entry)/R`
bearish: `(entry - Ask)/R`
Maintain flags:
`did1R`, `did2R`, `trailActive`
Actions:
When profitR >= 1 and not did1R:
partial close 0.25
SL = entry (breakeven)
When profitR >= 2 and not did2R:
partial close 0.25 of original (or of remaining—choose and be consistent)
SL = entry + sign1R
When profitR >= 3:
trail stop to: `SL = max(SL, entry + sign(floor(profitR)-1)R)`
(so at 3R -> SL at +2R? but PDF says “move SL up +1R for every +1R gains”; after +2R it was at +1R, so at +3R it becomes +2R, etc.)
B) Shield Protocol
From PDF:
move SL to breakeven when price reaches 80% in profit
trail SL after breaking significant structure with momentum by moving SL +1R per +1R gains
Ambiguity: “80% in profit” of what? TP distance? Usually yes.
Implement:
profitToTP = `abs(entry - TP)`
if `abs(current - entry) >= 0.8profitToTP` then SL=entry
Then trailing:
Only enable trailing after `StructureBreakWithMomentum()` event on M5
After enabled: same +1R step trail.
